250	381	She was the first Cypriot national and third woman to serve as President of the Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe.



381	581	Early life and education
Born in Nicosia, Kyriakides got a degree in psychology from the University of Reading and a master's degree in child maladjustment at the Victoria University of Manchester.



581	742	Early career
Kyriakides worked in the Ministry of Health between 1976 and 2006, as a clinical psychologist in the department of Child and Adolescent psychiatry.

742	832	In 1999 Kyriakides was elected as president of the First Breast Cancer Movement in Cyprus.
833	932	From 2004 until 2006, she served as president of the European Breast Cancer Coalition Europa Donna.
933	1030	In 2016, she was appointed President of the National Committee on Cancer Strategy of the Council.
1031	1133	Stella Kyriakides was also recognized as one of the 100 Influential Women in Oncology by OncoDaily.



